  "102|The Mortal Blade is an odachi capable of slaying the undying, and its crimson blade will take the life of any who dares draw it [2]. Without the power of Resurrection, one could not hope to wield this weapon, which allows one to defeat even infested beings [2]. It is required to draw Kuro's blood, one of the ingredients needed to reach the Divine Realm [2]. The blade gives Wolf the ability to sever the ties of immortality on creatures such as True Monk, Headless Ape, Hanbei the Undying, and Retrieving this item [2].": true,
  "103|In the Purification ending, Wolf beheads himself in order to sever the ties of immortality, freeing his Lord [1].": true,
  "104|Owl betrays Wolf because he believes \"The shinobi prosthetic... this was once... Curious device you have there\" [4] and wants to obtain the power of the Divine Heir's blood. When Owl orders Wolf to obey the Iron Code, he states \"As your father, I order you to forsake your master\" [3]. Wolf agrees by saying \"The code is absolute. I hereby forsake my master... the Divine Heir\" [3], which leads Owl to conclude \"With this, our supreme reign will...\" [3].": false,
  "105|The Corrupted Monk guards the entrance to the Wedding Cave Door where the Shelter Stone is enshrined [2]. She also served as the naginata wielding guardian of the Vermillion Bridge [1]. Her form appeared nebulous while guarding the Mibu Village cave entrance [3].": true,
  "106|Dogen created the original prosthetic arm for the Sculptor [3]. The Sculptor later passed this invention on to Wolf as his own left arm [2].": true,
  "107|Dragonrot spreads when one known to Wolf is coughing and wheezing, as it is likely they are afflicted with the sickness [1]. The illness manifests after Wolf perishes definitely four times, at which point he suffers a certain number of deaths he doesn't resurrect from [1]. This occurs because repeated use of the Dragon's Heritage leads to stagnation, which eventually reaches a point where it \"overflows\" and causes those who do not have the power to become sick [3].": false,
  "108|Emma made the Healing Gourd: \"The gourd of medicinal water you possess... That was originally a creation of mine\" [2].": true,
  "101|Owl found Sekiro and took him in as a foster son while having him trained (with the help of several co-mentors such as Lady Butterfly) to become a Shinobi [1]. Emma states that she was trained by Lord Isshin, but Wolf does not believe her skill counts as a mere passing interest [2].": false,
  "102|The Mortal Blade is an odachi capable of slaying the undying [3]. Its crimson blade will take the life of any who dares draw it [3]. Without the power of Resurrection, one could not hope to wield this weapon [3]. It allows one to defeat even infested beings [3]. The blade's true name is \"Gracious Gift of Tears\" [3]. It holds the power to open a gate to the underworld [1]. With it, you could kill one who cannot die through normal means [2].": false,
  "103|Wolf proceeds to behead himself in order to sever the ties of immortality, freeing his Lord [1].": true,
  "104|Owl betrays Wolf because he is driven by his own selfish goals of obtaining the Dragon's Blood [3]. Seduced by the Dragon's Heritage, Owl commands Wolf to obey the Iron Code and abandon Kuro [1]. After Wolf chooses to obey the Iron Code, Emma and Isshin will step in to stop him [1].": true,
  "105|The Corrupted Monk guards the entrance of the Wedding Cave Door [3]. She also serves as the naginata wielding guardian of the Vermillion Bridge [1]. Additionally, she guarded the bridge leading to the fountainhead palace [5].": false,
  "106|Dogen created the prosthetic arm for the Sculptor, and it later became the left arm given to Sekiro by the Sculptor [4]. Dogen is an extraordinary doctor and mechanical genius whose works include the Prosthetic Arm [2]. When the Sculptor lost his left arm, Dogen created that thing which has now become Wolf's left arm [5].": true,
  "107|Dragonrot spreads when one with the power of the Dragon's Heritage dies, causing the sickness known as Dragonrot to spread through the world [1]. The illness manifests after Wolf perishes definitely four times without being resurrected [1]. Repeated use of the Dragon's Heritage leads to stagnation, which eventually overflows and causes those without the power to become sick [4].": true,
  "108|Emma invented the Healing Gourd [4]. Emma states that the gourd was originally her creation intended for Lord Kuro [2].": true,
  "109|The provided wiki excerpts do not contain the name of Kuro's mother. My library doesn't cover that.": true,
  "102|The Mortal Blade is an odachi capable of slaying the undying [3]. Its crimson blade will take the life of any who dares draw it [3]. Without the power of Resurrection, one could not hope to wield this weapon, which allows one to defeat even infested beings [3]. It is said that with it, you could kill one who cannot die through normal means [2].": true,
  "103|In the Purification ending, Wolf \"proceeds to behead himself in order to sever the ties of immortality, freeing his Lord\" [1]. This action is part of the requirement where he must \"Choose to give Kuro the Divine Dragon's Tears and the Everblossom\" before sacrificing himself [3].": true,
  "104|Owl betrays Wolf because he is pursuing \"his own selfish goals of obtaining the Dragon's Blood\" [3]. After being seduced by the Dragon's Heritage, Owl commands Wolf to \"obey the Iron Code and abandon Kuro\" [1]. If Wolf chooses to obey, Emma and Isshin intervene to stop him, leading to a fight where Owl claims, \"Defeated by my own son? The feeling is not entirely unpleasant...\" [3].": false,
  "105|The Corrupted Monk guarded the entrance of the Wedding Cave Door [3]. She also watched over the cave entrance deep in Mibu Village [5]. Additionally, she was the naginata wielding guardian of the Vermillion Bridge [1].": true,
  "106|Dogen created the prosthetic arm, as stated by the Sculptor: \"When I lost my left arm, Dogen created that thing... which has now become your left arm\" [5]. The arm is also described as \"Dogen's legacy\" [5], and Sekiro was given it after originally losing his own arm to Genichiro Ashina [4].": true,
  "107|Dragonrot spreads when \"one with the power of the Dragon's Heritage dies,\" and \"the more one... dies, the more the sickness known as Dragonrot spreads through the world\" [1]. It specifically manifests after Wolf \"perishes definitely four times\" without resurrecting, as \"resurrecting does NOT cause Dragonrot\" [1]. Additionally, upon dying for the first time in New Game Plus, \"Dragonrot will spread\" regardless of previous deaths [2]. The illness occurs because \"repeated death causes the Dragon's Blood to stagnate,\" and if this stagnation reaches a point where it \"overflows,\" those without the power become sick [4].": true,
  "108|Emma invented the Healing Gourd: \"One of Dogen's apprentices, Emma, invented the Healing Gourd\" [4]. When Wolf asks if she made it, Emma confirms: \"Yes. It was intended for Lord Kuro\" [2].": true
